Make APC's Service dropdown a live, weight-aware lookup (v0.127)

Dan set an order to ND16 and noticed the Service dropdown only ever
offered Parcel-tier codes, even for a sub-1kg item where APC's own
rules also allow MailPack and CourierPack (cheaper products, same
next-day-by-16:00 slot). The v0.126 APC integration used a small
hand-picked list of Parcel codes as a placeholder rather than the
live ServiceAvailability.json lookup, explicitly flagged as a
follow-up in that release.

Implemented `ApcShippingService.checkServiceAvailability(order)`:
POSTs the order's actual delivery address + weight to
ServiceAvailability.json with Item/Type=ALL, so APC itself returns
every product family that genuinely fits (MailPack max 1kg,
CourierPack max 5kg, Standard Parcel max 30kg, per the guide's
Service Product Codes table) - exactly what the Hypaship website
shows. Mirrors DpdShippingService.listAvailableServices(order)
exactly, including the fallback shape: if the live call fails, falls
back to the last successfully-fetched list (cached in Settings as
apc_last_known_services), and only as a last resort to a small
static list. The order screen shows a Live/Cached badge, same as
DPD's dropdown already does.

Also: picking a service now saves its human description (e.g. "1600
Parcel") into the order's Service text, not just the raw product
code - previously only the code was stored, which is presumably
what read back as "ND-16" rather than "Next Day by 16:00".

